-- check/bad: a definition followed by a SEPARATE annotation with a
-- `where` clause: the annotation has no definition (it does not follow
-- one) and repeats the name. Both are the frontend's diagnostics; the checker
-- must add nothing and not fail. The bodyless annotation has no rigid
-- reading, so no givens, and elaboration (`Module.elaborate`) must not
-- assert that it has them.
less x y =
    x < y


less : a, a -> Bool where a.compare : a, a -> Order
